<h2>2. The Caesar cipher</h2>
<p>Each letter is moved k places along the alphabet, wrapping from Z to A. Other characters stay as they are. Decryption moves each letter back by k places. The key is the single number k, and anyone who knows k can both encrypt and decrypt.</p>
<p>With A = 0, B = 1, …, Z = 25: <code>E(m) = (m + k) mod 26</code> and <code>D(c) = (c − k) mod 26</code>.</p>
<label>Shift k (0 to 25) <input id="ckey" type="number" min="0" max="25" value="11"></label>
